\subsection{Results with Different Text Prompts}

Table~\ref{tab:kidney_segmentation} shows how segmentation performance varies with different text prompts for each kidney structure. Results indicate that the model is generally robust to prompt wording, with minor performance fluctuations. For example, for the Cortex, the DSC values varied between 70\% and 72\% for five different prompts. Prompts containing terms widely recognized in clinical contexts (``renal capsule'', ``renal cortex'') consistently perform well. Also, the capsule segmentation achieves higher performance (DSC 85–92\%, IoU 77–85\%) compared to the cortex, medulla, and central echo complex (DSC 66–73\%, IoU 50–58\%), suggesting that well-defined, clear anatomical boundaries (such as the capsule) are easier for SAM2 to segment accurately.


