\section{Scope and significance}\label{sec:def_sig}

In this section, we introduce the scope of SE for LLMs in \S\ref{sec:what_is_se4llm} and its significance in \S\ref{sec:why_is_se4llm}. 

% We begin by outlining the LLM development lifecycle, providing a concise overview of SE applications across different phases. We then explore the critical role of SE in four key areas: development, deployment, maintenance, and security, illustrating its fundamental importance in ensuring the reliability, efficiency, and scalability of LLMs.


\subsection{Scope}\label{sec:what_is_se4llm}

As summarized in \autoref{tab:software_vs_llm}, we can see that LLMs share similarities with traditional software while also exhibiting differences. Unlike traditional software, LLMs are built upon neural network architectures, resulting in non-deterministic outputs for identical inputs. Additionally, they differ from traditional software in terms of executability and testing methodologies. Despite these differences, LLMs retain many characteristics of traditional software.
% so that we can regard them as an emerging form of software to some extent. 
Given these hybrid characteristics, SE methodologies can be applied to enhance LLM in phases such as development, deployment, and maintenance. To systematically investigate this intersection, we explore how SE methodologies support various phases of the LLM development lifecycle, which consists of the phases illustrated in \autoref{fig:llm_lifecycle}:


