{\bf Structure of the paper.}
Section~\ref{sec:background} provides a review of the literature, divided into four subsections. Subsection~\ref{ssec:jailbreaking} discusses jailbreaking attacks, including those used in our multi-agent experiments and recent developments in the field. Subsection~\ref{ssec:priordef} reviews both traditional and emerging defence mechanisms against such attacks. The multi-agent LLM framework proposed in AutoDefense~\cite{zeng2024autodefense} is examined in Subsection~\ref{ssec:llmmulti}, while evaluation metrics for jailbreaking responses are covered in Subsection~\ref{ssec:Eval}. Section~\ref{sec:met} outlines the methodology used in our experiments, and Section~\ref{sec:res} presents the corresponding quantitative results. Section~\ref{sec:qual} discusses in depth the qualitative findings; this section analyses the misclassified data points and draws findings from them. The paper concludes with a summary of the findings in Section~\ref{sec:dis} and suggestions for future research in Section~\ref{sec:conclusion}.


