\subsection{Ablation Study}

\paragraph{Learning Rate.} To better illustrate how different training corpora impact forgetting, we increase the learning rate to $2 \times 10^{-5}$ and raise the batch size fourfold to amplify the effect of forgetting. As shown in Tab.~\ref{tab:2e5sft}, fine-tuning on the manually constructed SFT data causes catastrophic forgetting after just 300 steps, with performance on several tasks dropping to zero. In contrast, when fine-tuned on the correct GRPO rollouts, the model preserves much more of its original performance, even under this aggressive learning rate. Additionally, Fig.~\ref{fig:2e-5_trajectories} in Appendix~\ref{appendix:qualitative} plots the perplexity and task accuracy on the jigsaw-puzzle and grounding benchmarks during $100$, $200$, and $300$ training steps. Once again, the model fine-tuned on GRPO rollouts remains notably more stable at the higher learning rate.
